{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_019VssmoP6fvYpUXBiUiVp2G","type":"tool_result","content":"<persisted-output>\nOutput too large (66.7KB). Full output saved to: /Users/nick/.claude/projects/-Users-nick-code-roast-review/84d06975-53aa-44e0-a4d2-4df63462776f/tool-results/b4kilrek9.txt\n\nPreview (first 2KB):\ndiff --git a/AGENTS.md b/AGENTS.md\nindex 21f9f8f..834bab6 100644\n--- a/AGENTS.md\n+++ b/AGENTS.md\n@@ -65,6 +65,9 @@ here. This file holds only what most tasks hit.\n - The CLI parser preserves dashed option names and disables boolean\n   negation. Declare flags such as `no-browser` explicitly and read\n   `args['no-browser']`, rather than a camel-case property.\n+- `init` login-offer tests that use `simulateTerminals(t, true)` must\n+  pass `--finder-model` and `--verifier-model` flags, otherwise\n+  interactive prompts consume stdin before the login offers see it.\n - `simulateTerminals` only bypasses interactive-terminal detection. To\n   exercise raw-mode prompt input through the CLI, give stdin an `isTTY`\n   value of `true` and a `setRawMode` function; assert raw mode is restored.\ndiff --git a/README.md b/README.md\nindex 34e51f2..d7cb446 100644\n--- a/README.md\n+++ b/README.md\n@@ -82,17 +82,35 @@ model ID:\n   (`anthropic/claude-opus-5-5`, `meta-llama/llama-4:free`), uses\n   [OpenRouter](#openrouter).\n \n-Either model can fill either role. It's recommended to use models from different \n-providers for each role. For a model that no built-in provider serves,\n-edit `.roast.json` by hand (see [Project config](#project-config)).\n-Without the flags, `init` writes placeholder model IDs,\n-and a review refuses to run until you replace them in `.roast.json`.\n+Either model can fill either role. It's recommended to use models\n+from different providers for each role.\n+\n+In an interactive terminal, `init` prompts for each role's provider\n+and model when the corresponding flag is missing. The provider menu\n+lists Anthropic, OpenAI, and OpenRouter; each model prompt suggests a\n+default that Enter accepts. For a model that no built-in provider\n+serves, edit `.roast.json` by hand\n+(see [Project config](#project-config)).\n+\n+Without an interactive terminal, `init` writes placeholder model IDs\n+and prints a hint naming `--finder-model` and `--verifier-model`. A\n...\n</persisted-output>","is_error":false}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"84d06975-53aa-44e0-a4d2-4df63462776f","uuid":"a6aa6e47-813f-491e-a0d8-3705af449838","timestamp":"2026-11-24T23:27:23.210Z","tool_use_result":{"stdout":"diff --git a/AGENTS.md b/AGENTS.md\nindex 21f9f8f..834bab6 100644\n--- a/AGENTS.md\n+++ b/AGENTS.md\n@@ -65,6 +65,9 @@ here. This file holds only what most tasks hit.\n - The CLI parser preserves dashed option names and disables boolean\n   negation. Declare flags such as `no-browser` explicitly and read\n   `args['no-browser']`, rather than a camel-case property.\n+- `init` login-offer tests that use `simulateTerminals(t, true)` must\n+  pass `--finder-model` and `--verifier-model` flags, otherwise\n+  interactive prompts consume stdin before the login offers see it.\n - `simulateTerminals` only bypasses interactive-terminal detection. To\n   exercise raw-mode prompt input through the CLI, give stdin an `isTTY`\n   value of `true` and a `setRawMode` function; assert raw mode is restored.\ndiff --git a/README.md b/README.md\nindex 34e51f2..d7cb446 100644\n--- a/README.md\n+++ b/README.md\n@@ -82,17 +82,35 @@ model ID:\n   (`anthropic/claude-opus-5-5`, `meta-llama/llama-4:free`), uses\n   [OpenRouter](#openrouter).\n \n-Either model can fill either role. It's recommended to use models from different \n-providers for each role. For a model that no built-in provider serves,\n-edit `.roast.json` by hand (see [Project config](#project-config)).\n-Without the flags, `init` writes placeholder model IDs,\n-and a review refuses to run until you replace them in `.roast.json`.\n+Either model can fill either role. It's recommended to use models\n+from different providers for each role.\n+\n+In an interactive terminal, `init` prompts for each role's provider\n+and model when the corresponding flag is missing. The provider menu\n+lists Anthropic, OpenAI, and OpenRouter; each model prompt suggests a\n+default that Enter accepts. For a model that no built-in provider\n+serves, edit `.roast.json` by hand\n+(see [Project config](#project-config)).\n+\n+Without an interactive terminal, `init` writes placeholder model IDs\n+and prints a hint naming `--finder-model` and `--verifier-model`. A\n+review refuses to run until you replace the placeholders in\n+`.roast.json`.\n \n In the terminal, `init` then offers to log in to each provider\n that has no credential yet (see [Login and logout](#login-and-logout)).\n \n Flag `--no-login` skips the login process.\n \n+When the written config needs trust approval -- for example because it\n+names a custom endpoint or a non-standard credential variable -- `init`\n+prints a summary of every security-relevant value and asks whether to\n+approve. The default is No. Answering Yes records the approval so the\n+first review is not refused; answering No (or pressing Enter) skips\n+approval and `init` still succeeds. You can approve later with\n+`npx roast trust`. The trust offer only appears in an interactive\n+terminal.\n+\n \n #### `init` Example\n \ndiff --git a/docs/agents/config.md b/docs/agents/config.md\nindex 13ed0fe..dfe9b08 100644\n--- a/docs/agents/config.md\n+++ b/docs/agents/config.md\n@@ -46,10 +46,39 @@ flag, then config, then default).\n   pattern, minimum, required) go in the zod `.meta()`.\n - The `roast init` starter (`starter.ts`) shows commented-out defaults\n   from `defaults.ts`, the same module runtime settings use.\n-- The starter places a model by its ID alone (`placeModel`): a\n+- `starter()` takes a `StarterChoice` per role -- either a `RoleChoice`\n+  (provider + model) for built-in providers or a `CustomChoice`\n+  (endpoint, protocol, apiKeyEnv, model) for custom endpoints.\n+  `starterFromModels()` is the backward-compat wrapper that maps model\n+  strings onto choices via `placeModel` / `otherProvider`.\n+  `choiceFromModel()` builds a `RoleChoice` from a flag value.\n+- `placeModel` places a model by its ID alone: a\n   `<vendor>/<model>[:<variant>]` ID goes to OpenRouter, a bare ID to the\n-  provider `inferFamily` names. A placeholder role follows an OpenRouter\n-  role onto OpenRouter; otherwise it takes the other direct provider.\n+  provider `inferFamily` names. Custom model IDs skip `placeModel`\n+  entirely -- they stay on whatever custom endpoint the user typed. A\n+  placeholder role follows an OpenRouter role onto OpenRouter; otherwise\n+  it takes the other direct provider.\n+- Custom profile naming: a single custom role uses `custom`; when both\n+  roles are custom with different settings or models, they split to\n+  `custom-finder` and `custom-verifier`; identical settings share\n+  `custom`.\n+- Suggested model IDs for each built-in provider live in\n+  `SUGGESTED_MODELS` (`defaults.ts`). The `UnplaceableModelError`\n+  example text uses them so the two cannot drift.\n+- Interactive prompt flow lives in `src/cli/init.ts`:\n+  `promptRoleChoice` per role, calling `promptProvider` then\n+  `promptModel` (built-in) or `promptCustomEndpoint` (custom). The\n+  menu order is hardcoded in `PROVIDER_MENU` (Anthropic, OpenAI,\n+  OpenRouter, Custom endpoint). `suggestedModel()` picks the default\n+  from `SUGGESTED_MODELS`; for OpenRouter, it picks the slug for the\n+  vendor the other role is not using. A typed model at a built-in\n+  provider must pass `placeModel` and land on the chosen provider.\n+- When the finder chooses Custom, the verifier's default provider is\n+  also Custom, and its endpoint, protocol, and key variable prompts\n+  default to the finder's answers.\n+- After writing a config with custom endpoints, `init` offers trust\n+  approval (using `writeTrustSummary` and `promptNoDefault`) and prints\n+  a credential hint naming the variable to export.\n \n ## Providers\n \ndiff --git a/docs/agents/packaging.md b/docs/agents/packaging.md\nindex ff8b1a7..6ec5555 100644\n--- a/docs/agents/packaging.md\n+++ b/docs/agents/packaging.md\n@@ -58,3 +58,5 @@\n   publishes; `prepublishOnly` builds and runs `check:pack`. A failing\n   `prepublishOnly` after the tag is pushed is fixed by a follow-up patch\n   release, never by re-tagging.\n+- Update the suggested model IDs in `SUGGESTED_MODELS` (`defaults.ts`)\n+  and the README `init` example together when model names change.\ndiff --git a/src/cli/init.ts b/src/cli/init.ts\nindex 509cf01..36a34f4 100644\n--- a/src/cli/init.ts\n+++ b/src/cli/init.ts\n@@ -1,15 +1,35 @@\n // pattern: Imperative Shell\n import fs from 'node:fs/promises'\n import path from 'node:path'\n-import { starter, UnplaceableModelError } from '../config/starter.js'\n+import {\n+    starter, starterFromModels, UnplaceableModelError,\n+    choiceFromModel, otherProvider, placeModel,\n+    isCustomChoice,\n+    type RoleChoice, type CustomChoice, type StarterChoice,\n+} from '../config/starter.js'\n+import { roleKeyVar } from '../config/credential.js'\n+import { endpointProblem, PROTOCOLS } from '../config/endpoint.js'\n+import { SUGGESTED_MODELS } from '../config/defaults.js'\n import { PROJECT_CONFIG_NAME } from '../config/load.js'\n import { gitRoot } from '../git/git.js'\n+import { goTrimSpace } from '../gocompat/strings.js'\n import type { CommandDef, RunContext } from './command.js'\n import { loadProjectConfig } from './config.js'\n import { UsageError } from './errors.js'\n import { ensureStateIgnored, STATE_IGNORE_ENTRY } from './ignore.js'\n-import { loginPath, loginProvider, providersNeedingLogin } from './login.js'\n-import { interactiveTerminals, promptYesDefault } from './terminal.js'\n+import {\n+    loginPath, loginProvider, providersNeedingLogin,\n+} from './login.js'\n+import {\n+    requiresApproval, trustProjection,\n+    trustHash,\n+} from '../config/trust.js'\n+import { approve } from '../trust/trust.js'\n+import { writeTrustSummary } from './trust.js'\n+import {\n+    interactiveTerminals, promptYesDefault, promptNoDefault,\n+    type LineReader,\n+} from './terminal.js'\n \n export async function offerLogin (\n     file:string, ctx:RunContext\n@@ -41,13 +61,309 @@ export async function offerLogin (\n     }\n }\n \n+const CUSTOM_ENTRY = 'custom'\n+\n+const PROVIDER_MENU = [\n+    { num:'1', name:'anthropic' },\n+    { num:'2', name:'openai' },\n+    { num:'3', name:'openrouter' },\n+    { num:'4', name:CUSTOM_ENTRY },\n+]\n+\n+function suggestedModel (\n+    provider:string,\n+    otherChoice?:RoleChoice\n+):string {\n+    if (provider === 'openrouter') {\n+        const otherFamily = otherChoice?.provider === 'openai' ?\n+            'openai' : 'anthropic'\n+        return otherFamily === 'openai' ?\n+            SUGGESTED_MODELS.openrouter[1] :\n+            SUGGESTED_MODELS.openrouter[0]\n+    }\n+    return SUGGESTED_MODELS[\n+        provider as 'anthropic'|'openai'\n+    ] ?? ''\n+}\n+\n+function defaultProvider (\n+    role:'finder'|'verifier',\n+    otherChoice?:StarterChoice\n+):string {\n+    if (role === 'finder') return 'openai'\n+    if (otherChoice && isCustomChoice(otherChoice)) {\n+        return CUSTOM_ENTRY\n+    }\n+    return otherChoice ?\n+        otherProvider(\n+            (otherChoice as RoleChoice).provider\n+        ) : 'anthropic'\n+}\n+\n+function parseProviderInput (input:string):string|null {\n+    const trimmed = goTrimSpace(input).toLowerCase()\n+    if (trimmed === '') return null\n+    const byNum = PROVIDER_MENU.find(p => p.num === trimmed)\n+    if (byNum) return byNum.name\n+    const byName = PROVIDER_MENU.find(p => p.name === trimmed)\n+    if (byName) return byName.name\n+    return null\n+}\n+\n+async function promptProvider (\n+    out:NodeJS.WritableStream,\n+    lines:LineReader,\n+    role:'finder'|'verifier',\n+    otherChoice?:StarterChoice\n+):Promise<string|null> {\n+    const def = defaultProvider(role, otherChoice)\n+    const menu = PROVIDER_MENU.map(p =>\n+        `  ${p.num}. ${p.name}${p.name === def ?\n+            ' (default)' : ''}`\n+    ).join('\\n')\n+    for (;;) {\n+        out.write(\n+            `\\n${role} provider:\\n${menu}\\n` +\n+            `Choose [${def}]: `\n+        )\n+        const answer = await lines.readLine()\n+        if (answer === null) return null\n+        const trimmed = goTrimSpace(answer)\n+        if (trimmed === '') return def\n+        const provider = parseProviderInput(trimmed)\n+        if (provider) return provider\n+        out.write(\n+            'invalid choice; enter a number (1-' +\n+            `${PROVIDER_MENU.length}) or a provider name\\n`\n+        )\n+    }\n+}\n+\n+async function promptModel (\n+    out:NodeJS.WritableStream,\n+    lines:LineReader,\n+    role:'finder'|'verifier',\n+    provider:string,\n+    otherChoice?:RoleChoice\n+):Promise<string|null> {\n+    const suggested = suggestedModel(provider, otherChoice)\n+    for (;;) {\n+        out.write(`${role} model [${suggested}]: `)\n+        const answer = await lines.readLine()\n+        if (answer === null) return null\n+        const trimmed = goTrimSpace(answer)\n+        if (trimmed === '') return suggested\n+        const placed = placeModel(trimmed)\n+        if (placed === provider) return trimmed\n+        out.write(\n+            `model does not place onto ${provider}; ` +\n+            'use a model ID for that provider\\n'\n+        )\n+    }\n+}\n+\n+const KEY_VAR_RE = /^[A-Z_][A-Z0-9_]*$/\n+\n+async function promptCustomEndpoint (\n+    out:NodeJS.WritableStream,\n+    lines:LineReader,\n+    role:'finder'|'verifier',\n+    otherChoice?:StarterChoice\n+):Promise<CustomChoice|null> {\n+    const defaults = otherChoice &&\n+        isCustomChoice(otherChoice) ? otherChoice : null\n+\n+    let endpoint:string\n+    const defEndpoint = defaults?.endpoint ?? ''\n+    for (;;) {\n+        const hint = defEndpoint ?\n+            ` [${defEndpoint}]` : ''\n+        out.write(`endpoint URL${hint}: `)\n+        const answer = await lines.readLine()\n+        if (answer === null) return null\n+        const trimmed = goTrimSpace(answer)\n+        if (trimmed === '' && defEndpoint) {\n+            endpoint = defEndpoint\n+            break\n+        }\n+        const problem = endpointProblem(\n+            role, trimmed, 'chat', 1\n+        )\n+        if (!problem) { endpoint = trimmed; break }\n+        out.write(problem + '\\n')\n+    }\n+\n+    let protocol:string\n+    const defProtocol = defaults?.protocol ?? 'chat'\n+    for (;;) {\n+        out.write(`protocol [${defProtocol}]: `)\n+        const answer = await lines.readLine()\n+        if (answer === null) return null\n+        const trimmed = goTrimSpace(answer)\n+        if (trimmed === '') { protocol = defProtocol; break }\n+        if ((PROTOCOLS as readonly string[]).includes(\n+            trimmed\n+        )) {\n+            protocol = trimmed\n+            break\n+        }\n+        out.write(\n+            'protocol must be chat, responses, ' +\n+            'or anthropic\\n'\n+        )\n+    }\n+\n+    let apiKeyEnv:string\n+    const defKey = defaults?.apiKeyEnv ?? ''\n+    const keyHint = defKey ? ` [${defKey}]` : ''\n+    for (;;) {\n+        out.write(\n+            `key variable name${keyHint} ` +\n+            '(blank for role default): '\n+        )\n+        const answer = await lines.readLine()\n+        if (answer === null) return null\n+        const trimmed = goTrimSpace(answer)\n+        if (trimmed === '' && defKey) {\n+            apiKeyEnv = defKey; break\n+        }\n+        if (trimmed === '') { apiKeyEnv = ''; break }\n+        if (KEY_VAR_RE.test(trimmed)) {\n+            apiKeyEnv = trimmed; break\n+        }\n+        out.write(\n+            'key variable must match ' +\n+            '[A-Z_][A-Z0-9_]*\\n'\n+        )\n+    }\n+\n+    out.write(`${role} model: `)\n+    const modelAnswer = await lines.readLine()\n+    if (modelAnswer === null) return null\n+    const model = goTrimSpace(modelAnswer)\n+\n+    return {\n+        kind:'custom',\n+        endpoint,\n+        protocol,\n+        apiKeyEnv,\n+        model,\n+    }\n+}\n+\n+async function promptRoleChoice (\n+    out:NodeJS.WritableStream,\n+    lines:LineReader,\n+    role:'finder'|'verifier',\n+    otherChoice?:StarterChoice\n+):Promise<StarterChoice|null> {\n+    const provider = await promptProvider(\n+        out, lines, role, otherChoice\n+    )\n+    if (provider === null) return null\n+    if (provider === CUSTOM_ENTRY) {\n+        return promptCustomEndpoint(\n+            out, lines, role, otherChoice\n+        )\n+    }\n+    const model = await promptModel(\n+        out, lines, role, provider,\n+        otherChoice && !isCustomChoice(otherChoice) ?\n+            otherChoice : undefined\n+    )\n+    if (model === null) return null\n+    return { provider, model }\n+}\n+\n+function sameSetup (\n+    a:StarterChoice, b:StarterChoice\n+):boolean {\n+    if (a.model !== b.model) return false\n+    if (isCustomChoice(a) && isCustomChoice(b)) {\n+        return a.endpoint === b.endpoint &&\n+            a.protocol === b.protocol\n+    }\n+    if (isCustomChoice(a) || isCustomChoice(b)) return false\n+    return a.provider === b.provider\n+}\n+\n+async function offerTrust (\n+    file:string, repo:string, ctx:RunContext\n+):Promise<void> {\n+    try {\n+        const cfg = await loadProjectConfig(file, ctx)\n+        const p = trustProjection(cfg)\n+        if (!requiresApproval(p)) return\n+        if (!interactiveTerminals(ctx.stdin, ctx.stderr)) {\n+            ctx.stderr.write(\n+                'run `npx roast trust` to approve ' +\n+                'the config\\n'\n+            )\n+            return\n+        }\n+        writeTrustSummary(ctx.stderr, p)\n+        if (!await promptNoDefault(\n+            ctx.stderr, ctx.lines,\n+            'Trust this project config?'\n+        )) {\n+            ctx.stderr.write(\n+                'run `npx roast trust` later to ' +\n+                'approve\\n'\n+            )\n+            return\n+        }\n+        await approve(repo, trustHash(p), {\n+            env:ctx.env as NodeJS.ProcessEnv,\n+            signal:ctx.signal,\n+        })\n+        ctx.stderr.write(\n+            'Approved for this clone.\\n'\n+        )\n+    } catch (err) {\n+        ctx.stderr.write(\n+            `trust: ${String(err)}\\n`\n+        )\n+    }\n+}\n+\n+export async function writeStarterFromChoices (\n+    cwd:string,\n+    finder:StarterChoice,\n+    verifier:StarterChoice\n+):Promise<string> {\n+    const file = path.resolve(cwd, PROJECT_CONFIG_NAME)\n+    const body = starter(finder, verifier)\n+    let handle:fs.FileHandle\n+    try {\n+        handle = await fs.open(file, 'wx', 0o644)\n+    } catch (err) {\n+        if ((err as NodeJS.ErrnoException).code === 'EEXIST') {\n+            throw new UsageError(`${file} already exists; edit it, ` +\n+                'or remove it to start over', { cause:err })\n+        }\n+        throw new Error(`create ${file}: ${String(err)}`, { cause:err })\n+    }\n+    try {\n+        await handle.writeFile(body)\n+    } catch (err) {\n+        await handle.close().catch(() => {})\n+        throw new Error(`write ${file}: ${String(err)}`, { cause:err })\n+    }\n+    try {\n+        await handle.close()\n+    } catch (err) {\n+        throw new Error(`close ${file}: ${String(err)}`, { cause:err })\n+    }\n+    return file\n+}\n+\n export async function writeStarter (\n     cwd:string, finderModel:string, verifierModel:string\n ):Promise<string> {\n     const file = path.resolve(cwd, PROJECT_CONFIG_NAME)\n     let body:string\n     try {\n-        body = starter(finderModel, verifierModel)\n+        body = starterFromModels(finderModel, verifierModel)\n     } catch (err) {\n         if (!(err instanceof UnplaceableModelError)) throw err\n         throw new UsageError(`--${err.role}-model: ${err.message}`,\n@@ -106,14 +422,142 @@ export const initCommand:CommandDef = {\n             if (ctx.signal.aborted) throw err\n             throw new UsageError(String(err), { cause:err })\n         }\n-        const file = await writeStarter(ctx.cwd,\n-            args['finder-model'] as string, args['verifier-model'] as string)\n-        ctx.stdout.write(`wrote ${file}\\n`)\n-        const ignored = await ensureStateIgnored(repo)\n-        if (ignored.added) {\n-            ctx.stdout.write(`added ${STATE_IGNORE_ENTRY} ` +\n-                `to ${ignored.path}\\n`)\n+        const configPath = path.resolve(\n+            ctx.cwd, PROJECT_CONFIG_NAME\n+        )\n+        try {\n+            await fs.access(configPath)\n+            throw new UsageError(\n+                `${configPath} already exists; edit it, ` +\n+                'or remove it to start over'\n+            )\n+        } catch (err) {\n+            if (err instanceof UsageError) throw err\n+        }\n+        const finderFlag = goTrimSpace(\n+            args['finder-model'] as string\n+        )\n+        const verifierFlag = goTrimSpace(\n+            args['verifier-model'] as string\n+        )\n+        const interactive = interactiveTerminals(\n+            ctx.stdin, ctx.stderr\n+        )\n+        const needFinderPrompt = !finderFlag && interactive\n+        const needVerifierPrompt = !verifierFlag && interactive\n+        if (!interactive && (!finderFlag || !verifierFlag)) {\n+            const hints:string[] = []\n+            if (!finderFlag) hints.push('--finder-model')\n+            if (!verifierFlag) hints.push('--verifier-model')\n+            ctx.stderr.write(\n+                'no interactive terminal; pass ' +\n+                hints.join(' and ') +\n+                ' to set models\\n'\n+            )\n+        }\n+        let finderChoice:StarterChoice\n+        let verifierChoice:StarterChoice\n+        if (needFinderPrompt || needVerifierPrompt) {\n+            if (needFinderPrompt) {\n+                const choice = await promptRoleChoice(\n+                    ctx.stderr, ctx.lines, 'finder'\n+                )\n+                if (choice === null) return\n+                finderChoice = choice\n+            } else {\n+                try {\n+                    finderChoice = choiceFromModel(\n+                        'finder', finderFlag\n+                    )\n+                } catch (err) {\n+                    if (err instanceof UnplaceableModelError) {\n+                        throw new UsageError(\n+                            `--finder-model: ${err.message}`,\n+                            { cause:err }\n+                        )\n+                    }\n+                    throw err\n+                }\n+            }\n+            if (needVerifierPrompt) {\n+                const choice = await promptRoleChoice(\n+                    ctx.stderr, ctx.lines, 'verifier',\n+                    finderChoice!\n+                )\n+                if (choice === null) return\n+                verifierChoice = choice\n+            } else {\n+                try {\n+                    const other = isCustomChoice(finderChoice!) ?\n+                        undefined : finderChoice! as RoleChoice\n+                    verifierChoice = choiceFromModel(\n+                        'verifier', verifierFlag, other\n+                    )\n+                } catch (err) {\n+                    if (err instanceof UnplaceableModelError) {\n+                        throw new UsageError(\n+                            '--verifier-model: ' +\n+                            err.message,\n+                            { cause:err }\n+                        )\n+                    }\n+                    throw err\n+                }\n+            }\n+            if (sameSetup(finderChoice!, verifierChoice!)) {\n+                ctx.stderr.write(\n+                    '\\nnote: both roles use the same model' +\n+                    ' -- verification adds little in ' +\n+                    'that setup\\n'\n+                )\n+            }\n+            const file = await writeStarterFromChoices(\n+                ctx.cwd, finderChoice!, verifierChoice!\n+            )\n+            ctx.stdout.write(`wrote ${file}\\n`)\n+            const ignored = await ensureStateIgnored(repo)\n+            if (ignored.added) {\n+                ctx.stdout.write(`added ${STATE_IGNORE_ENTRY}` +\n+                    ` to ${ignored.path}\\n`)\n+            }\n+            for (const [role, choice] of [\n+                ['finder', finderChoice!],\n+                ['verifier', verifierChoice!],\n+            ] as const) {\n+                if (isCustomChoice(choice)) {\n+                    const varName = choice.apiKeyEnv ||\n+                        roleKeyVar(role)\n+                    ctx.stderr.write(\n+                        `export ${varName} to supply ` +\n+                        `the ${role} credential\\n`\n+                    )\n+                }\n+            }\n+            if (!args['no-login']) {\n+                await offerLogin(file, ctx)\n+            }\n+            await offerTrust(file, repo, ctx)\n+        } else {\n+            let file:string\n+            try {\n+                file = await writeStarter(\n+                    ctx.cwd, finderFlag, verifierFlag\n+                )\n+            } catch (err) {\n+                if (err instanceof UsageError) throw err\n+                throw err\n+            }\n+            ctx.stdout.write(`wrote ${file}\\n`)\n+            const ignored = await ensureStateIgnored(repo)\n+            if (ignored.added) {\n+                ctx.stdout.write(\n+                    `added ${STATE_IGNORE_ENTRY}` +\n+                    ` to ${ignored.path}\\n`\n+                )\n+            }\n+            if (!args['no-login']) {\n+      