{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-4-6","id":"msg_011ChNd2y73EeL6aQqhAUqPz","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"So `SUGGESTED_MODELS.openrouter[0]` = `'anthropic/claude-opus-5-5'` and `[1]` = `'openai/gpt-6.1-terra'`.\n\nThe logic in `suggestedModel`:\n- other role is on OpenAI -> `otherFamily = 'openai'` -> returns `openrouter[1]` = `'openai/gpt-6.1-terra'`\n\nThis suggests an OpenAI-vendor model when the other role is already using OpenAI. That's the opposite of what the spec wants.\n\nThe spec says: \"choosing the vendor the other role is not using.\" So if the other role is on OpenAI, OpenRouter should suggest `anthropic/claude-opus-5-5` (index 0), not `openai/gpt-6.1-terra` (index 1).\n\nThis is a correctness bug. The return logic is inverted.\n\nLet me also quickly verify there's no test that would catch this:\n\nThe test at `test/cli/init.ts:268` (\"init prompts provider by number and accepts suggested model\") iterates over providers and uses an `otherNum` that's the complement. For openrouter (num='3'), `otherNum` is also '3'. So the other choice for openrouter tests would be openrouter itself, which doesn't exercise the cross-vendor logic meaningfully.\n\nLet me now check for one more thing -- the `starterFromModels` backward-compat function:"}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":1,"cache_creation_input_tokens":865,"cache_read_input_tokens":76856,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":865,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0},"output_tokens":3,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"global","speed":"standard"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":"toolu_01NoWnxGniRCCzNW5rfoVfsx","agent_id":"adc0a41f1fc4a8870","session_id":"84d06975-53aa-44e0-a4d2-4df63462776f","uuid":"3228ed14-97ec-4bff-b7c3-5c6a2236690f","timestamp":"2026-11-24T23:29:29.467Z","request_id":"req_011ChNd2y25UadrheNuw9