{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-4-6","id":"msg_011ChNdCqVfhnKfUVZwFN5Fq","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Tests are running. While they finish, let me compile my findings. Let me re-verify the `suggestedModel` logic one more time:\n\n```ts\nfunction suggestedModel (\n    provider:string,\n    otherChoice?:RoleChoice\n):string {\n    if (provider === 'openrouter') {\n        const otherFamily = otherChoice?.provider === 'openai' ?\n            'openai' : 'anthropic'\n        return otherFamily === 'openai' ?\n            SUGGESTED_MODELS.openrouter[1] :   // openai/gpt-6.1-terra\n            SUGGESTED_MODELS.openrouter[0]      // anthropic/claude-opus-5-5\n    }\n```\n\nWhen `otherChoice?.provider === 'openai'`:\n- `otherFamily = 'openai'`\n- returns `SUGGESTED_MODELS.openrouter[1]` = `'openai/gpt-6.1-terra'`\n\nThe other role IS using OpenAI, and we're suggesting an OpenAI-vendor model on OpenRouter. The spec says \"choosing the vendor the other role is not using.\" So we should return `anthropic/claude-opus-5-5` (index 0) instead.\n\nWhen `otherChoice?.provider !== 'openai'` (e.g., anthropic):\n- `otherFamily = 'anthropic'`\n- returns `SUGGESTED_MODELS.openrouter[0]` = `'anthropic/claude-opus-5-5'`\n\nThe other role IS using Anthropic, and we're suggesting an Anthropic-vendor model on OpenRouter. Again wrong.\n\nThe fix would be to swap: when other is OpenAI -> suggest anthropic slug (index 0); when other is anthropic -> suggest openai slug (index 1).\n\nAlso, the spec says \"finder defaults to the Anthropic slug when the verifier is not yet known.\" When `otherChoice` is undefined (finder prompt, verifier not yet known): `otherFamily = 'anthropic'`, returns `openrouter[0]` = `'anthropic/claude-opus-5-5'`. That part IS correct.\n\nWait, let me re-read more carefully. The variable is named `otherFamily` but it represents the family of the OTHER role. The intent seems like it should pick the same family as the other role to AVOID overlap... no, actually the naming is confusing.\n\nActually, I think the intent is: `otherFamily` is what family to pick for the OpenRouter suggestion. But the naming and logic are both inverted. The variable should be named something like `suggestFamily`, and when the other role is on OpenAI, we should suggest the non-OpenAI family.\n\nThe code returns the SAME vendor as the other role for OpenRouter, which defeats the spec's purpose of using different providers.\n\nNow let me also check the `profileNames` dead code:\n\nAt `starter.ts:193-201`:\n```ts\nif (fCustom && vCustom) {\n    const same = sameCustom(finder, verifier)\n    if (same && finderModel === verifierModel) {\n        return ['custom', 'custom']\n    }\n    if (same) {\n        return ['custom-finder', 'custom-verifier']\n    }\n    return ['custom-finder', 'custom-verifier']\n}\n```\n\nLines 198-199 and 200-201 are identical branches. Not a bug (the result is correct per spec) but dead code.\n\nLet me now write the findings file."}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":1,"cache_creation_input_tokens":376,"cache_read_input_tokens":78617,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":376,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0},"output_tokens":1,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"global","speed":"standard"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":"toolu_01NoWnxGniRCCzNW5rfoVfsx","agent_id":"adc0a41f1fc4a8870","session_id":"84d06975-53aa-44e0-a4d2-4df63462776f","uuid":"1da39605-0c95-48cc-b4fc-c8c94afb719a","timestamp":"2026-11-24T23:31:51.211Z","request_id":"req_011ChNdCqRD3ru4yzoq9Gkn4","subagent_type":"fork","task_description":"Read and analyze test diffs"}
