{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-4-6","id":"msg_011ChNdczkTZmomPH2URxkWf","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"I need to write this from the parent context since I'm a fork. Let me report back.\n\nTwo correctness findings:\n\n1. **`suggestedModel` OpenRouter vendor logic is inverted** (`src/cli/init.ts:76-80`): When `otherChoice.provider` is `'openai'`, `otherFamily` becomes `'openai'` and the function returns `SUGGESTED_MODELS.openrouter[1]` (`openai/gpt-6.1-terra`) -- the same vendor as the other role. The spec says \"choosing the vendor the other role is not using.\" The default case (no `otherChoice`, i.e. finder prompt) correctly returns the anthropic slug, but once the other role is known the ternary picks the same vendor instead of the opposite. Example: finder on OpenAI, verifier picks OpenRouter -- suggested model is `openai/gpt-6.1-terra` instead of `anthropic/claude-opus-5-5`.\n\n2. **Custom endpoint model prompt lacks validation** (`src/cli/init.ts:240-243`): The spec requires \"any non-empty trimmed string with no whitespace or control characters\" but `promptCustomEndpoint` just trims and accepts whatever the user typed -- including internal spaces, tabs, or control characters. No validation loop like the other custom-endpoint prompts have."}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":1,"cache_creation_input_tokens":471,"cache_read_input_tokens":81974,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":471,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0},"output_tokens":1,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"global","speed":"standard"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":"toolu_01NoWnxGniRCCzNW5rfoVfsx","agent_id":"adc0a41f1fc4a8870","session_id":"84d06975-53aa-44e0-a4d2-4df63462776f","uuid":"9084ab91-5e98-4736-9e3f-26a88dfdf231","timestamp":"2026-11-24T23:37:08.664Z","request_id":"req_011ChNdczfW8tWmLqg